# §13d G2–G4 statement gate: cut checks and landed forms

Tool: `bash <S>/tools/leanelab.sh <OUT>/work/base <S>/oleans-lmain <file>` (direct `lean`, no `-o`, no
olean written). Base: <OUT>/work/base, a read-only `git archive` export of the campaign tip 6672531c (after #105,
the merge to main); its `.lake` is a symlink to <S>/wt-mig1tip's packages (same `lake-manifest.json`). Snapshot:
`oleans-lmain` (the root replay at ff2d6f6b, Lean-equal to the tip). Toolchain: `leanprover/lean4:v4.25.0`.
<OUT> is the landing folder; <S> the scratchpad. Run: 2026-10-15 17:54 UTC.

`python3 -I <OUT>/scripts/cutcheck.py <OUT>/G24Statements.lean <OUT>/base <OUT>/cut` (the C1 and
stage-2 gates' script, verbatim) writes, for each part, a file holding the imports of the part's import
closure and the bodies of the parts in that closure, in file order. Each is elaborated on its own.
